-- title:
--   Smooth chart points lie on the ε_∞-component of geometric fibres
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a modulus $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is trivial, and a witness `hj` that the Laurent series $j$-expansion `jqModC ℚ` lies in the field $\mathbb{Q}$-generated by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms for $SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be an `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, that is, the bundled arithmetic data on the two-chart model $X$ of the $\Gamma_H(M)$ function field over $R_p$ (properness, flatness, integrality, normality, the smooth $\Gamma_N$-model, an identification of the geometric generic fibre with a curve model of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-function field together with its Galois equivariance, smoothness and geometric integrality of the generic fibre, a section $\varepsilon_\infty$, a smooth locus and the distinguished closed subcurves `𝔛.comp`). Let $f \in R_p$ and let $v$ be an element of the finite chart algebra `chartAlgFin p (ΓM M H) hj` (the elements of the function field integral over $R_p[j]$). Assume the dictionary hypothesis `hdict`: for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$ and with algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$, every ring homomorphism $\rho : R_p \to A$ compatible with the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every point $y$ of the fibre of $X$ along the residue composite of $\rho$, and every prime $\mathfrak{q}$ of the finite chart algebra, if $y$ projects to the point $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}(\mathfrak{q})$ of $X$ and $v \notin \mathfrak{q}$, then $y$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,0$ and not in the image of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,1$. Finally let $k$ be an algebraically closed field, $s : \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} R_p[1/f]$ a geometric point, $y$ a point of the fibre at $s$ of the base change of $X$ to $R_p[1/f]$, and $\mathfrak{q}$ a prime of the finite chart algebra with $v \notin \mathfrak{q}$ and with $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}(\mathfrak{q})$ in $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{smoothLocus}$, such that the composite of the two first projections sends $y$ to $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}(\mathfrak{q})$. The conclusion is that $y$ lies in the connected component, within the open preimage of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{smoothLocus}$ under that composite projection, of the image of the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} k$ under the section point obtained from $\varepsilon_\infty$ by base change to $R_p[1/f]$ and then specialisation along $s$.
--
--   This is the geometric-fibre component statement for the $\Gamma_H$-model at $p$: away from the locus cut out by $v$, smooth points of the finite chart of any geometric fibre lie on the same connected component of the smooth locus as the cusp section $\varepsilon_\infty$. It feeds the construction of a one-sided pool of points over the base change $R_p[1/f]$, used in the analysis of the reduction of $X_H$ at $p$.
